{
  "id": "cai",
  "term": "CAI",
  "definition": "CAI means cast-as-intended verifiability in electronic voting: a safeguard that lets a voter check that the vote recorded matches the vote they meant to cast, even without a secure channel to election officials. In this source, it is discussed as a security and trust property that can be difficult to balance with protection against coercion.",
